# BENCH-83 confirmation on the Windows PC (issue #151, docs/bench/live-3.10.md): the 11 opponents
# the bench crippled, against 3.10 built from master, 4 seeds of 35 rounds. Close the RoboRumble
# client shards first.  Run from hadur-bench:  .\queue.ps1 run confirm-fix-310   (or ./queue.sh)
#
# Pass: no battle logs "Preventing ... META-INF" (analyse.py marks such a row "JDK resource
# denied"), and each robot's score moves from its crippled bench mean towards its live score
# (the role column of crippled-310.txt holds both). Frankie, VertiLeach, Princess, LauLectrik,
# Nibbler and Griffon were 15 to 28 points easier on the crippled bench than live.

set COMMON = --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant 1488498 --child-heap 2G --engine 1.11.1
set C310 = --robot-jar ../hadur-robot/target/hadur2.Hadur_3.10.jar --robot "hadur2.Hadur 3.10"

prep | (cd .. && mvn -q -B package -DskipTests) && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set crippled-310.txt

confirm-310 | ./bench-top20.sh --skip-build ${COMMON} --set crippled-310.txt --seeds 4 ${C310} --label confirm-fix-310
  after: prep
